      "Name": "body",
      "Html": "\u003Cstyle class=\u0022code-analysis-syntax\u0022\u003E\n.docs-content pre{overflow-x:auto;margin:1rem 0 1.75rem;padding:1.25rem 1.4rem;border:1px solid rgba(20,42,72,.16);border-left:4px solid #0e6fae;border-radius:4px;background:#f7fbfe;color:#10263a}\n.docs-content pre code{white-space:pre;color:inherit;background:transparent;font-size:1rem;line-height:1.65}\n.language-csharp .syntax-comment{color:#587287;font-style:italic}.language-csharp .syntax-string{color:#8a3d12}.language-csharp .syntax-keyword{color:#6542a6;font-weight:700}.language-csharp .syntax-number{color:#096b65}.language-csharp .syntax-type{color:#0a6680;font-weight:600}\n\u003C/style\u003E\u003Cheader class=\u0022docs-page-header\u0022\u003E\u003Ch1\u003E[page[title]]\u003C/h1\u003E\u003Cp\u003EAn exposure must not contain loops.\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/header\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EWhat the Standard says\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u0026ldquo;Pure Mapping\u0026rdquo; \u0026mdash; Exposure components only map communication between an external caller and the core business service. They do not call brokers, make business decisions, iterate, or sequence multiple business routines. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://github.com/hassanhabib/The-Standard/blob/master/3.%20Exposers/3.%20Exposers.md#3000-pure-mapping\u0022 target=\u0022_blank\u0022 rel=\u0022noreferrer\u0022\u003Eread it here\u003C/a\u003E.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EWhy it matters\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003ELooping in an exposure turns request translation into workflow processing. Passing the request to a business service keeps iteration, failure handling, and operation semantics consistent across every exposure.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EBad code example\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cpre\u003E\u003Ccode class=\u0022language-csharp\u0022\u003E\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-comment\u0022\u003E// Violates STXE002: An exposure must not contain loops.\u003C/span\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Easync\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EValueTask\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EPost\u003C/span\u003E(\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EStudent\u003C/span\u003E[] students)\n{\n    \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Eforeach\u003C/span\u003E (\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EStudent\u003C/span\u003E student \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Ein\u003C/span\u003E students)\n    {\n        \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Eawait\u003C/span\u003E service.\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EAddStudent\u003C/span\u003E(student);\n    }\n}\u003C/code\u003E\u003C/pre\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EGood code example\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cpre\u003E\u003Ccode class=\u0022language-csharp\u0022\u003E\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-comment\u0022\u003E// Follows STXE002\u003C/span\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EValueTask\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EPost\u003C/span\u003E(\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EStudent\u003C/span\u003E[] students) =\u0026gt; service.\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EAddStudents\u003C/span\u003E(students);\u003C/code\u003E\u003C/pre\u003E"
    }
